    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0308" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/2042f</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chinese Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Koo</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 82</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On July 10, 1918, I had the honor to
                    communicate to you copies of confidential letters exchanged between certain
                    American bankers and myself on the subject of the formation of an American group
                    for the purpose of rendering financial assistance to China.</p>
                <p>I have the honor now to enclose herewith for your information and for the
                    information of your Government copy of an identic note with accompanying
                    memorandum on the above-mentioned subject, which I have to-day handed to the
                    representatives of Great Britain, France and Japan.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d191-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
